BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:casa-de-velazquez-artists-in-residence-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART:20261127T113000Z
DTEND:20261127T120000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 13:00 CET: Casa de Velazquez: Artists in Residence 2027-20
 28 (Academie de France a Madrid)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 27 Nov 2026 at 13:00 CET.\n\nThe Academie de France a Ma
 drid at the Casa de Velazquez offers 12 one-year residencies for 2027-2028
  to young graduates and established artists developing a creative project 
 in the Iberian Peninsula.\n\nOrganisation: Casa de Velazquez\, Academie de
  France a Madrid\nLocation: Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velaz
 quez). No nationality requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affi
 liated to an artist/author or self-employed scheme in their country of res
 idence\, and non-EU applicants need a French residence permit allowing wor
 k or a Schengen work and residence permit from another EU state. Good Fren
 ch required.\nAward: Monthly residency grant voted each year\; for 2026-20
 27 it was EUR 3\,600 per month for artists housed at the Casa and EUR 4\,6
 00 per month for artists living outside (with children). Twelve monthly pa
 yments\, September 2027 to August 2028. Housing and studio provided\; a pr
 oduction support fund is also available on project. No application fee.\nD
 uration: 12 months (1 September 2027 to 31 August 2028\; on site mid-Septe
 mber to about 20 July)\n\nMore: https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-e
 n-la-casa/detail/appel-artistes-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-en-la-casa/detail/appel-artist
 es-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velazquez). No nationalit
 y requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affiliated to an artist/
 author or self-employed scheme in their country of residence\, and non-EU 
 applicants need a French residence permit allowing work or a Schengen work
  and residence permit from another EU state. Good French required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART:20261106T123000Z
DTEND:20261106T130000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 CET: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Resid
 encies 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Nov 2026 at 14:00 CET.\n\nThe European Media Art Plat
 form (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of leading European media-art organisations
  offering fully funded two-month production residencies for artists workin
 g with digital media\, including media art\, bio art and robotic art.\n\nO
 rganisation: European Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-mon
 th production residency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, Fr
 ance\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 
 4\,000 grant for the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 
 for a collaborating artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 proje
 ct budget\; accommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU cei
 lings\; access to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Two months\n\nMore: https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:est-nord-est-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: Est-Nord-Est Artist Residency 2027-2028 (Saint-Jean-Port-
 Joli\, Quebec)
DESCRIPTION:Est-Nord-Est offers eight-week residencies in Saint-Jean-Port-J
 oli\, Quebec\, welcoming professional visual artists\, whether established
  or emerging\, from Quebec\, Canada and other countries\, with four artist
 s per season.\n\nOrganisation: Est-Nord-Est\, residence d'artistes\nLocati
 on: Saint-Jean-Port-Joli\, Quebec\, Canada. Open to professional visual ar
 tists\, established or emerging\, from Quebec\, Canada and other countries
 \; materials\, travel and additional living expenses are the resident's ow
 n responsibility.\nAward: CAD 2\,080 residency honorarium\, plus a free in
 dividual studio-workshop with lodging\, access to specialized wood\, metal
  and ceramics equipment\, a documentation center\, and technical\, artisti
 c and logistical support. Four artists per session. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Eight weeks. Sessions: Spring 19 April - 11 June 2027\; Summer 5 
 July - 27 August 2027 (curated\, priority to artists of African descent)\;
  Fall 27 September - 19 November 2027\; Winter 24 January - 18 March 2028.
 \n\nMore: https://estnordest.org/en/artist-residency/artist-residency-regu
 lar/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://estnordest.org/en/artist-residency/artist-residency-regular/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Saint-Jean-Port-Joli\, Quebec\, Canada. Open to professional visua
 l artists\, established or emerging\, from Quebec\, Canada and other count
 ries\; materials\, travel and additional living expenses are the resident'
 s own responsibility.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi Museum: SIXI AiR Open Call 2027 Spring & Autumn (Nan
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:The Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project\, run by Six
 i Museum in Nanjing since 2024\, selects 4 artists across two three-month 
 sessions in 2027 (Spring\, March to May\, and Autumn\, September to Novemb
 er).\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: Nanjing\, China. Open to arti
 sts of all disciplines and cultural backgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, profi
 cient in Mandarin or English.\nAward: Round-trip flights\, visa applicatio
 n fees\, insurance\, and a private city-center apartment or loft studio on
  the outskirts\, plus a material allowance (amount not published)\, techni
 cal assistance\, airport pickup and translation support. NO artist fee or 
 stipend mentioned. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: Spring 202
 7 (March to May) or Autumn 2027 (September to November).\n\nMore: https://
 siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China. Open to artists of all disciplines and cultural b
 ackgrounds\, aged 18 or older\, proficient in Mandarin or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
