BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dca-near-coup-grants-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: LA Department of Cultural Affairs: NEAR + CO-UP Artist Re
 sidency Grants 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The City of Los Angeles' residency-based grant line for sociall
 y engaged art. Neighborhood Engagement Artist Residencies (NEAR\, USD 12\,
 000) fund individual teaching-artists to run participatory\, multi-session
  residency projects in self-selected non-arts venues (community organizati
 ons\, civic spaces) across LA's Council Districts\, reaching audiences wit
 h little exposure to arts programming.\n\nOrganisation: City of Los Angele
 s Department of Cultural Affairs (DCA)\nLocation: Los Angeles\, US. Reside
 ncies take place in non-arts venues across the City of Los Angeles\; for L
 A-based artists and partner organizations.\nAward: NEAR grants of USD 12\,
 000 for individual artists\; CO-UP grants of USD 15\,000 for collaboration
 s between social-justice nonprofits and artists. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Multi-session residencies during the 2027-28 cycle\n\nMore: https://
 culture.lacity.gov/grants/near-co-op?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.lacity.gov/grants/near-co-op?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Los Angeles\, US. Residencies take place in non-arts venues across
  the City of Los Angeles\; for LA-based artists and partner organizations.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adkx-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163800Z
DTSTART:20261211T213000Z
DTEND:20261211T220000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 EST: Adirondack Experience (ADKX) Artist-in-Residenc
 e 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 11 Dec 2026 at 17:00 EST.\n\nThe Adirondack Experience m
 useum on Blue Mountain Lake offers four one-month artist residencies for J
 une\, July\, August and September 2027. Residents work publicly on their o
 wn practice a minimum of six hours a day (roughly 10:00-16:00) three days 
 a week in the museum's public areas\, and spend two days a week (Fridays a
 nd Saturdays\, 10:00-16:30) engaging visitors in the Art Lab makerspace.\n
 \nOrganisation: Adirondack Experience\, The Museum on Blue Mountain Lake (
 ADKX)\nLocation: Blue Mountain Lake\, New York\, USA. Open internationally
